# --- IG Publisher / SUSHI build artifacts (regenerated on every build) ---
# The generated IG website. Never commit it; previews are published via CI.
output/
# IG Publisher scratch space.
temp/
# The template package the IG Publisher extracts into ./template at build
# time. Why: this repo REFERENCES the template by version in ig.ini; the
# extracted copy is a build artifact. (A deliberate vendored bring-up copy
# would live under a different, tracked path.)
template/
# Downloaded FHIR package cache.
input-cache/
# FSH -> FHIR JSON output generated by SUSHI.
# TEMPORARILY TRACKED (2026-09-02): the ballot is released through Simplifier,
# which reads the generated FHIR resources out of the repository, so they have
# to be committed. This reverses the migration's decision (commit c163838) for
# as long as that holds. Re-enable the line below once the release path moves to
# this repository's own publication pipeline, and untrack the directory again.
# fsh-generated/
#
# Restores exactly what was tracked before c163838 — resources/ and includes/,
# but not SUSHI's two build indices, which churn on every run and carry nothing
# Simplifier needs.
fsh-generated/data/
fsh-generated/fsh-index.txt
# The IG Publisher's generated per-resource translation TEMPLATES (json/po/xliff),
# regenerated on every build. Root-anchored ON PURPOSE: an unanchored
# `translations/` would also match input/translations/, which is the tree this
# module MAINTAINS and must keep tracked.
/translations/
# The IG Publisher jar itself — downloaded, version-pinned, never committed.
publisher.jar

# --- Tooling ---
node_modules/

# --- OS / editor noise ---
.DS_Store
*.log

# The migration run's RAW per-step tool output: the multi-megabyte publisher and
# SUSHI transcripts. Everything that summarises them - run.log, the
# measurements, the page map, the verification findings, the report - IS
# committed. The negation below is load-bearing: the `*.log` rule under "OS /
# editor noise" above would otherwise swallow run.log, which is the audit trail
# every claim in the migration report traces to.
migration-log/*.log
!migration-log/run.log
migration-log/*.prev.log
